From: Personal OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Add built-in driver firmware to Dakota's GNOME initramfs

Dakota owns our GNOME junction, so carry the fix as one more patch in its
gnome-build-meta queue. The queued patch explains the change itself.

diff --git a/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-initramfs-firmware.patch b/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-initramfs-firmware.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9269048
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/gnome-build-meta/personal-os-initramfs-firmware.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Upstream-Status: Pending
+Exit: Drop when gnome-build-meta's initramfs ships firmware for built-in drivers.
+Subject: initramfs: include firmware requested by built-in drivers
+
+Built-in drivers request their firmware before the root filesystem is
+mounted, so it has to be in the initramfs. The lookup only tried `.xz`,
+while freedesktop-sdk ships firmware compressed with zstd or uncompressed,
+so every entry was skipped. Try the same extensions as copy-initramfs.py.
+
+Built-in cfg80211 also loads regulatory.db at boot and never retries, so
+Wi-Fi stayed on the restrictive world regulatory domain. Add
+wireless-regdb-bin to the initramfs so the lookup can find it.
+
+diff --git a/elements/oci/initramfs/deps.bst b/elements/oci/initramfs/deps.bst
+index 8646bc8..92d46b6 100644
+--- a/elements/oci/initramfs/deps.bst
++++ b/elements/oci/initramfs/deps.bst
+@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ depends:
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/tpm2-tools.bst
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/tzdata.bst
+ - freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/util-linux.bst
++- freedesktop-sdk.bst:components/wireless-regdb-bin.bst
+ - freedesktop-sdk-extra.bst:components/zram-generator.bst
+ - gnomeos-deps/plymouth-gnome-theme.bst
+ - gnomeos-deps/udev-hide-usr.bst
+diff --git a/files/gnomeos/generate-initramfs/modules/50-kmod/module.sh b/files/gnomeos/generate-initramfs/modules/50-kmod/module.sh
+index 113e082..0c0720f 100644
+--- a/files/gnomeos/generate-initramfs/modules/50-kmod/module.sh
++++ b/files/gnomeos/generate-initramfs/modules/50-kmod/module.sh
+@@ -80,13 +80,14 @@ install() {
+     while IFS= read -r -d '' line; do
+         case "${line}" in
+             *.firmware=*)
+-                firmware="${line##*.firmware=}"
+-                path="/usr/lib/firmware/${firmware}.xz"
+-                if [ -f "${path}" ]; then
+-                    install_file "${path}"
+-                else
+-                    echo "Ignoring missing ${path}"
+-                fi
++                firmware="/usr/lib/firmware/${line##*.firmware=}"
++                for path in "${firmware}" "${firmware}.xz" "${firmware}.zst"; do
++                    if [ -f "${path}" ]; then
++                        install_file "${path}"
++                        continue 2
++                    fi
++                done
++                echo "Ignoring missing ${firmware}"
+                 ;;
+         esac
+     done <"/usr/lib/modules/${kernelver}/modules.builtin.modinfo"
